# FindGood agent rules

Inspect `ARCHITECTURE.md` and the owning module before writing code. Search for an existing service, repository, protocol, or component. Do not duplicate behavior.

## Ownership

- HTTP routes validate and delegate. No business rules, no SQL.
- Domain logic lives in `services/backend/app/domain`. It must not import FastAPI.
- Persistence goes through repositories in `app/db/repositories`.
- Ingestion adapters stay in `app/ingestion`. Fetchers do not parse or publish.
- Frontend feature UI lives in `apps/web/src/features`. Shared chrome in `components`.
- External vendors (maps, analytics, geocoding) stay behind one adapter.

If you cannot name the owning module, do not start coding.

## Hard constraints

- Never silently change API contracts. Additive fields only unless the user explicitly asks for a break.
- Never publish unvalidated crawler output. Candidates are intermediate; publishing is explicit.
- Never overwrite `SourceSnapshot` rows. They are immutable evidence.
- Preserve Deal → publication → snapshot → source → URL provenance.
- Schema changes need an Alembic revision. Do not edit applied migrations.
- Money is `Decimal` / `Numeric`. Never floats.
- Schedule math honors the venue location timezone. Never assume UTC equals local time.
- Do not add dependencies that the current stack already covers.
- Do not place secrets in frontend bundles or source control.

## After a change

- Update tests when behavior changes.
- Run the relevant pytest module and/or frontend typecheck/tests before claiming completion.
- Report exactly which files changed and why.
- Document material architectural decisions in `ARCHITECTURE.md`.
